course: dictionary
lesson: 3003
title: During: when something happens
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: During is a small word that tells you when something happens. It is a preposition, so it is usually followed by a time or an event: during the night, during dinner, during the game.
explain: During has two meanings. It can mean all through a time, as in «during the night», where the whole night is covered. It can also mean at some point in a time, as in «He called during dinner», where the call happened once while dinner was going on. Ask yourself: did it last the whole time, or did it happen at one moment inside it?
explain: The words around during give the clues. «Lifeguards move the flags during the day, because the safe place changes as the tide and currents change.» The flags are moved at different times across the day, because the sea keeps changing, so during tells you when the moving happens.
fact: During is a preposition: it tells you when something happens.
fact: «During the night» means all through the night.
fact: «He called during dinner» means at some point while dinner was going on.
fact: During is followed by a time or an event, such as during the week, during the game or during class.
fact: Check the meaning by swapping in another word, such as while or throughout. If the sentence still makes sense, you have understood during.
exercise: «During the night, the house was very quiet.» What does during mean here? | *All through the night | Before the night began | Only for one minute of the night | After the morning came
exercise: «He called during dinner.» Did he call all through dinner or at some point while dinner was going on? | *At some point while dinner was going on | After dinner had finished | All through dinner, from start to finish | Before dinner started
exercise: «Lifeguards move the flags during the day.» What time is named after during? | *the day | safe | move | the flags
test: «Lifeguards move the flags during the day, because the safe place changes as the tide and currents change.» Why do lifeguards move the flags during the day? | *Because the safe place changes as the tide and currents change | Because it is night and the beach is empty | Because the flags are old and torn | Because they are bored of the same spot
test: Which sentence uses during to mean all through a time? | *The baby slept soundly during the whole night | Ella phoned during the game | Tom sneezed during the film | The bus came during lunch
exam: «Chest pain or fainting during sport is never normal.» What does during sport mean here? | Only after sport has finished | Instead of doing sport | For exactly one hour of sport | *At any point while a person is doing sport
